%S A401525 2,3,4,0,1,5,4,4,5,8,5,7,0,4,2,1,6,0,5,7,3,5,2,7,8,4,1,2,9,9,0,7,4,3,
%T A401525 7,7,8,2,6,9,9,6,9,7,6,3,0,5,3,6,8,9,9,0,4,5,0,0,5,3,6,2,1,8,3,0,1,4,
%U A401525 6,9,6,3,6,3,1,1,7,4,2,3,0,8,5,2,8,4,8,9,5,0,2,2,8,2,7,8,3,1,8,1,9,6,7,4,6
%N A401525 Decimal expansion of liminf_{N->oo} log(N)*(E - E(N)), where E is the Shannon entropy of Benford's law and E(N) is the Shannon entropy of the leading decimal digit of a random integer k in 1..N chosen with probability proportional to 1/k.
%C A401525 Let P_d(N) = (Sum_{1<=k<=N, k has leading decimal digit d} 1/k) / (Sum_{1<=k<=N} 1/k), the probability that a random integer k in 1..N, chosen with probability proportional to 1/k, has leading decimal digit d. By Duncan's theorem, P_d(N) -> p(d) = log_10(1+1/d) as N -> oo (Benford's law).
%C A401525 E(N) = -Sum_{d=1..9} P_d(N)*log(P_d(N)) and E = -Sum_{d=1..9} p(d)*log(p(d)) = 1.99343315079120426982... . For every N >= 1, E(N) < E (Khomyakov, Theorem 3.1(iii)).
%C A401525 The deficit E - E(N) is of exact order 1/log(N), and log(N)*(E - E(N)) oscillates: its liminf is this constant, the limit along N = 10^K, and its limsup is A401526 = 0.88767826374..., the limit along N = 3*10^K (Khomyakov, Theorem 4.3(b) and Corollary 4.4).
%H A401525 R. L. Duncan, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/00150517.1969.12431129">Note on the initial digit problem</a>, Fibonacci Quart. 7 (1969), 474-475.
%H A401525 Vladimir Khomyakov, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23660786">The harmonic leading-digit law is one-sided at every N</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A401525 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benford%27s_law">Benford's law</a>.
%F A401525 Equals Sum_{d=1..9} (R(d) - gamma*p(d))*log(p(d)), where p(d) = log_10(1+1/d), R(d) = Sum_{j>=0} (psi((d+1)*10^j) - psi(d*10^j) - log(1+1/d)), gamma is Euler's constant (A001620) and psi is the digamma function.
%F A401525 R(d) = Sum_{j>=0} (H((d+1)*10^j - 1) - H(d*10^j - 1) - log(1+1/d)), where H(n) is the n-th harmonic number, and Sum_{d=1..9} R(d) = gamma.
%F A401525 Equals Sum_{k=1..8} log(p(k)/p(k+1))*M(k+1), where M(t) = Sum_{j>=0} (psi(t*10^j) - (1-x)*psi(10^j) - x*psi(10^(j+1))) and x = log_10(t); M(2) = A401527.
%e A401525 0.234015445857042160573527841299074377826996976305368990450053...
%o A401525 (Python) # via mpmath; D = Sum_{d=1..9} (R(d) - gamma*p(d))*log(p(d)), p(d) = log_10(1+1/d)
%o A401525 from mpmath import mp, mpf, log, digamma, euler
%o A401525 digits = 105          # number of digits to compute; the only parameter to change
%o A401525 mp.dps = digits + 20  # working precision: 20 guard digits
%o A401525 J = digits + 20       # number of terms of R(d): 0 <= R(d) - (sum over j < J) < 10^-J
%o A401525 def p(d): return log(1 + mpf(1)/d)/log(10)
%o A401525 def R(d): return sum(digamma(mpf(d+1)*10**j) - digamma(mpf(d)*10**j) - log(1 + mpf(1)/d) for j in range(J))
%o A401525 D = sum((R(d) - euler*p(d))*log(p(d)) for d in range(1, 10))
%o A401525 print(", ".join(str(int(D*10**digits))))  # first `digits` digits of D = 0.2340..., truncated
%Y A401525 Cf. A401526 (limsup), A401527, A001620, A007524.
%K A401525 nonn,cons,new
%O A401525 0,1
%A A401525 _Vladimir Khomyakov_, Oct 28 2026
